      "name": "Write",
      "arguments": {
        "file_path": "/tmp/bd_mem_r1.txt",
        "content": "Meridian Credits release 1.0 credit agreement (finance-approved in issue trial-351, 2026-09-07; statement-total command approved in issue trial-eio, 2026-09-08; statement receipts approved in issue trial-ep6, 2026-09-08). Applies to Meridian Credits quote, total, and statement requests naming release 1.0 explicitly. Since issue trial-0gf (2026-09-08) the current agreement is release 2.0, so an omitted release selects 2.0 (see meridian-credits/release-2.0-credit-agreement); before trial-0gf an omitted release selected 1.0 (see meridian-credits/current-agreement-history). Versions introduced in an issue remain supported afterward.\n\nCredit rules per request (a request is the complete charge set of one independently quoted monthly statement; caps apply within that set):\n- Uncapped credit per line: 10% of charge_cents, rounded down separately per line to integer cents (integer arithmetic charge_cents // 10).\n- Cap: 2400 cents shared by ALL lines with the same account_id, across its subscriptions; distinct account_id groups have independent caps.\n- Assignment priority within a cap group: earliest service_on first; equal service dates use increasing line_id (lexicographic = Unicode code-point order).\n- Each line receives its uncapped credit up to the group remaining cap; later lines receive only the remainder, or zero.\n- Totals: total credit = sum of assigned line credits; per-line amount due = charge - assigned credit; total due = total charges - total credit.\n\nOne-line quote contract (trial-351): request {\"command\":\"quote\",\"line\":LINE} or same with \"release\":\"1.0\"; response has exactly release, line_id, credit_cents, amount_due_cents; the supplied line is treated as the entire statement. Example: charge 19999 -> credit 1999, due 18000.\n\nStatement total contract (trial-eio): request {\"command\":\"total\",\"lines\":[LINE,...]} or same with \"release\":\"1.0\"; response has exactly release, credit_cents, amount_due_cents for the whole supplied charge set under this agreement shared-cap scope; it is NOT a collection of independent single-line quotes. Empty lines -> {\"release\":\"1.0\",\"credit_cents\":0,\"amount_due_cents\":0}; a statement of only the quote example line (charge 19999) -> credit 1999, due 18000. The quote command remains available and unchanged.\n\nStatement receipts contract (trial-ep6): request {\"command\":\"statement\",\"release\":\"1.0\",\"lines\":[LINE,...]} returns itemized receipts under the original finance-approved release 1.0 agreement with its cap scope (per account_id across subscriptions) and line-credit priority (earliest service_on, then increasing line_id) unchanged. Response has exactly release (\"1.0\"), lines, credit_cents, amount_due_cents; each lines entry has exactly line_id, credit_cents, amount_due_cents with the line's assigned credit and per-line due = charge - assigned credit; the response preserves the input line order, which is independent of the priority order; overall credit_cents and amount_due_cents equal the total command for the same input. Empty lines -> {\"release\":\"1.0\",\"lines\":[],\"credit_cents\":0,\"amount_due_cents\":0}. One-line receipt of the quote example (charge 19999) -> lines entry {\"line_id\":\"L-1\",\"credit_cents\":1999,\"amount_due_cents\":18000} with overall credit 1999, due 18000. Current statement behavior remains release 2.0; existing quote and total release support is unchanged. (Statement dispatch accepting \"1.0\" first shipped in trial-gy1 as an inference; trial-ep6 is its explicit approval - no agreement text changed.)\n\nLine schema constraints: exactly line_id, account_id, subscription_id, service_on, charge_cents; IDs nonempty strings; line_id unique within a request; subscription identified by (account_id, subscription_id) pair; service_on valid Gregorian YYYY-MM-DD in 2020-01-01..2099-12-31; charge_cents nonnegative integer US cents; no line excluded by service date; line collections may be empty; JSON key order immaterial; no response keys beyond those specified.\n\nCLI contract: python3 main.py reads one JSON object on stdin, writes exactly one JSON object on stdout. {\"command\":\"ping\"} -> {\"status\":\"ok\",\"product\":\"Meridian Credits\"}; unknown command -> {\"error\":\"unknown_command\"}. No network/clock/locale/third-party packages; malformed input out of scope.\n\nImplementation notes beyond the agreement text (inference, not finance-approved): main.py implements the full multi-line assignment (assign_credits_release_1_0) so the shared-cap priority order is available to all commands; statement_release_1_0 builds per-line results from the same map total uses, so statement and total cannot diverge; a release value outside SUPPORTED_RELEASES (\"1.0\",\"2.0\") returns {\"error\":\"unsupported_release\"} for quote, total, and statement alike. For a single account group the total assigned credit equals min(sum of per-line uncapped credits, 2400) regardless of assignment order, because greedy assignment saturates the cap; priority order still governs per-line assignment.\n\nVerification (2026-09-08): public suites public_tests/release_1_quote.json and public_tests/release_1_total.json pass (python3 test_public.py --cases); local release-1.0 cases in tests/test_quote.py and tests/test_total.py pass. Re-verified 2026-09-08 in issue trial-0gf after release 2.0 became the current agreement: explicit-1.0 public suites and local release-1 tests still pass unchanged alongside the release-2 suites. Re-verified 2026-09-08 in issue trial-ep6: public suite public_tests/release_1_statement.json (one-line receipt) passes and all release-1.0 statement cases in tests/test_statement.py pass (empty statement, service-date/line-id priority with input order preserved, overall amounts equal total), alongside all five public suites and all 40 local tests.\n\nSource: issues trial-351 and trial-eio quoting the finance-approved release 1.0 agreement and the approved statement-total contract; statement receipts contract quoted from issue trial-ep6; current-agreement revision in issue trial-0gf."
      },
